+### 4.3 list_sessions
+
+Requests summaries of the conversations owned by the authenticated WebSocket user. The server takes the user id from the connection and MUST ignore any `userId` field in the frame; the client cannot list another user's conversations ([validated by: answers list_sessions for the authenticated user with ISO dates, forwarding limit and before while ignoring any client userId](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L97)).
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "list_sessions",
+  "limit": 10,
+  "before": {"updatedAt": "2026-01-01T00:05:00.000Z", "sessionId": "s3"}
+}
+```
+
+| Field    | Type   | Required | Description |
+| -------- | ------ | -------- | ----------- |
+| `type`   | string | Yes      | `"list_sessions"` |
+| `limit`  | number | No       | Non-negative integer page size |
+| `before` | object | No       | Cursor containing `updatedAt` and `sessionId` from the last row received |
+
+The validator rejects a non-integer or negative `limit`, and a cursor without a 1–128 character `sessionId` or a parseable `updatedAt`, with `INVALID_MESSAGE` before the store is called ([validated by: accepts a bare list_sessions frame and rejects a malformed limit or before with INVALID_MESSAGE without calling listFor](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L167)).
+
+Listing is answered outside the per-session turn lock, so it can complete while a user message is streaming. A store without `listFor` answers `UNSUPPORTED`; a store failure answers `SERVER_ERROR` and leaves the socket open ([validated by: refuses a conversation list when the store cannot list it](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L107)).
+
 ## 5. Server-to-Client Messages

 ### 5.1 connected
@@ -312,6 +334,7 @@ Defined error codes:
 | `INVALID_FORMAT`  | Message body is not valid JSON                                    |
 | `RATE_LIMITED`    | AI provider returned a rate limit error                           |
 | `SERVER_ERROR`    | Unexpected server error during message processing                 |
+| `UNSUPPORTED`     | The requested optional store capability is unavailable             |

 Semantics:

@@ -357,6 +380,24 @@ Semantics:
 - The client SHOULD use this message to clear any "processing" or "loading" indicators.
 - The client MUST treat a run as complete only at `stream_end` or when the socket closes. Unparseable JSON is the one frame answered with `INVALID_FORMAT` and no `stream_end`, because the server cannot tell what it was meant to be; for it the client falls back on the socket closing.

+### 5.9 session_list
+
+Carries the requested user's conversation summaries. It is sent only in response to `list_sessions`; the server does not push it unsolicited.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "session_list",
+  "sessions": [{"sessionId": "s2", "createdAt": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z", "updatedAt": "2026-01-01T00:02:00.000Z", "entryCount": 4}]
+}
+```
+
+| Field      | Type     | Description |
+| ---------- | -------- | ----------- |
+| `type`     | string   | `"session_list"` |
+| `sessions` | object[] | Summaries in newest-activity-first order |
+
+Each summary contains only `sessionId`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt` and `entryCount`; the two times are ISO-8601 strings and no conversation content or credentials are included ([validated by: answers list_sessions for the authenticated user with ISO dates, forwarding limit and before while ignoring any client userId](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L97)). A client can reconnect with `?sessionId=<sessionId>` to resume a selected conversation when resume is enabled; the existing ownership check applies.
+
 ## 6. SessionEntry Objects

 A SessionEntry represents a single piece of content in the conversation. Every entry has a `role` field that determines its shape. The `role` acts as a discriminant for the union type.
